{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Approved batch implementation kickoff\n\nThe implementation epic is cepivorous-dynamitic-deer at origin/main commit ce496143fe1f72a07efeb0173da37013262ec446. It has exactly eleven approved children. Each child has binary acceptance criteria, declared file impact or an explicit no-file-impact reason, and executable verification commands.\n\n- F14 is grayish-deceased-puppy.\n- F15 is helpful-stale-wildcat.\n- F16 is disposable-unacademic-millipede.\n- F17 is obeliskoid-thorium-goose.\n- F18 is immolated-holohedral-waterdogs.\n- F20 is fleshless-gray-weasel.\n- F29 is upperclass-aquamarine-whippet.\n- F30A is herby-crude-rat.\n- F30B is peppery-dire-indianabat.\n- F31 is uneducated-tinned-yapok.\n- F38 is childless-rhyolite-puma.\n\nF17 depends on F15 so both use one identity contract. F30B depends on F30A because both edit docs/architecture.md. All other children are independent. F05 remains deferred. F02, F03, and F04 remain rejected. F23 and the lower README rewrite remain held. No child adds mechanical prose or character enforcement.\n\nA production ticket write failed once with `fatal: unable to write new index file`. Exact searches found only closed tickets for a test-only cause and different write-fault signatures. The distinct production failure is recorded as scary-fiscal-grunion, linked discovered_from this epic and related to the prior retry tickets. The identical F30B create succeeded after the tracker was clean.\n\nPlan review will run in dependency order. Every leaf will be claimed before repository edits or gates. Repository units will land independently through Gerrit after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments. Markdown-only units will use focused documentation and contract checks without the full test suite. F14 will run the default test suite because it changes checker behavior."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787516975688304001,"uuid":"3574cc66-0112-41ee-a570-f9bac2e005f1"}